The Separation Trap: In logistic regression, if a symptom separates the groups too cleanly (e.g., every single patient with BP >160 had a stroke, and nobody with BP ≤160 did), the logistic S-curve tries to become infinitely steep. The weights blow up toward ±∞ and the computer crashes. Bayes doesn't care—it just models the shape of each mountain independently.   
